| ID | Title | Severity |
|----|-------|----------|
| F001 | HTTP TRACE Method Enabled on IIS Services | 🟢 Low |
| F002 | Default IIS Landing Page Exposed | ℹ️ Info |
| F003 | Potential WSUS Service Exposed on Port 8530 | ℹ️ Info |
| **F004** | **Plaintext Service Credential Exposed in Readable Log Share** | **🟠 High** |
| **F005** | **Domain Users Can Create Machine Accounts (MAQ = 10)** | **🟡 Medium** |

### Finding F004 — Deep Dive

The `Logs` SMB share was readable by any authenticated user and contained IdentitySync application logs with **plaintext Active Directory credentials**:

```
BindUser: LOGGING\svc_recovery
BindPass: Em3rg3ncyPa$$2025
```

**Impact:** Any authenticated domain user can recover service credentials → lateral movement to read gMSA passwords → DA compromise via WSUS spoofing.

### Finding F005 — Deep Dive

`ms-DS-MachineAccountQuota` was set to 10 (default), allowing any authenticated user to create computer accounts. This enabled:
1. Creating `CERTIFRIED$` for initial exploration
2. Creating `ATTACKER01$` for DNS record manipulation

